Notebook[{
Cell["HypergraphRule", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"c55681b3-ec49-b24c-b979-941a6753cc7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"HypergraphRule", "[", 
    RowBox[{"input", ",", " ", "output"}], "]"}], "InlineCode"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"9a4e75ec-70f8-b142-ba6c-f734b695b9ef"],
 " ",
 "represents the rewrite rule taking the hypergraph input to the hypergraph \
output."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"77fee413-e1b5-c34b-b709-6e6751c69354"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"b88fdc76-7bb0-1746-b3cd-dd6487e2e451"],

Cell["\<\
Either side may be given as anything Hypergraph accepts, and is converted; a \
side that is not a hypergraph gives HypergraphRule::hg.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8c3906b1-b8cc-c140-8e47-c6b1c31fe565"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"rule", "[", "hg", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"6a72faf4-8993-924a-8c32-1ae7ce433b20"],
 " applies the rule, giving one event for every way the input matches. See ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["HypergraphRuleApply", "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"9ec82653-a976-774f-ae2a-40b73964b704"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"d75e0087-5dd5-4b45-bcb6-99ab9297b206"],

Cell["\<\
A vertex of the input that the output keeps is carried through the rewrite; \
one the output introduces is created fresh; one the output drops is \
destroyed. \"SharedVertices\", \"NewVertices\" and \"DeletedVertices\" report \
the three groups, read off the two sides by vertex identifier.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"76dec01e-888d-1740-8c43-dd9bc83fd472"],

Cell["\<\
Vertices correspond between the two sides by identifier, so the same name on \
both sides means the same vertex, and a name on the output alone means a new \
one.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fc455098-9180-364f-b373-afd0d3c0c590"],

Cell["\<\
The shape follows the reference paclet this package grew out of, so that \
rules written for that one read the same here.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"2e799845-d1bd-a140-855d-a37371221cee"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"3c8d4ec4-36d9-034d-8dd2-4eccf1781cc5"],

Cell["\<\
Subdividing an edge: the two endpoints are kept, a third vertex is new.\
\>", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"46fcb3ea-675a-c844-9015-f12bf3f5b14f"],

Cell["sub = HypergraphRule[{{1, 2}}, {{1, 3}, {3, 2}}]", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"eaa5016f-3d51-3e41-add6-1e609acaf811"],

